#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105401 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7c9317eb-d1ce-5f42-b69b-a37e643b865b" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Vector Projection Using Angle and Magnitude"}] :question/id #uuid "3278333b-a29e-54c5-bc94-b5525bc6f751" :question/math-academy-id "e-14617" :question/problem "Suppose that $|\\,\\mathbf{a}\\,|=8,|\\,\\mathbf{b}\\,|=4$ and that the angle between the vectors is $\\theta = \\dfrac{5\\pi}{6}.$ Find the vector projection of $\\mathbf{a}$ onto $\\mathbf{b}$ in terms of the vector $\\mathbf{b}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the scalar projection as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{b}\\,a & =|\\,a\\,|\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =8\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{5\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =8\\cdot (-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}) \\\\  & =-4\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the unit vector that is parallel to $\\mathbf{b}\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{u} = \\dfrac{\\mathbf{b}}{|\\,\\mathbf{b}\\,|} = \\dfrac{\\mathbf{b}}{4} = \\dfrac{1}{4} \\mathbf{b}\n$$\n\nFinally, we compute the vector projection as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{b}\\,a & ={\\text{comp}}_{b}\\,a\\cdot u \\\\  & =-4\\sqrt{3}\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}b \\\\  & =-\\sqrt{3}b\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105402 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c0670172-77cb-5e88-b78d-e5136c06095f" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Vector Projection Using Components"}] :question/id #uuid "58b2269d-f998-5ba5-9df8-54ea422c43aa" :question/math-academy-id "e-14618" :question/problem "Let $\\mathbf{a}=\\langle 1,-3,5 \\rangle$ and $\\mathbf{b}=\\langle 5,-4,0 \\rangle$. Find the vector projection of $\\mathbf{a}$ onto $\\mathbf{b}$." :question/worked-solution "Using the formula for the vector projection, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{b}\\,a & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{b\\cdot b}b \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{x}{b}_{x}+{a}_{y}{b}_{y}+{a}_{z}{b}_{z}}{{b}_{x}^{2}+{b}_{y}^{2}+{b}_{z}^{2}}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot 5+(-3)\\cdot (-4)+5\\cdot 0}{{5}^{2}+(-4)^{2}+{0}^{2}}b \\\\  & =\\frac{17}{41}⟨5,-4,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{85}{41},-\\frac{68}{41},0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105403 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "84c96375-27d5-5ada-a952-34e09b3e92bf" :knowledge-point/title "Perpendicular Vectors"}] :question/id #uuid "663f3f5e-56cf-5517-ba1e-d1a355767e0b" :question/math-academy-id "e-14619" :question/problem "Let ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046753/assets/e199e48633dbaeeb817da846163a9c8a9bf1ae3355c69b56461b25a13ef73406.png) and ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046753/assets/4ce6e454ff96976ddeb735d1ab42562fe3b7eb16f16e7c0402d8040f9586907b.png). Find the vector projection of $\\mathbf{a}$ onto $\\mathbf{b}$." :question/worked-solution "Using the formula for the vector projection, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{b}\\,a & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{b\\cdot b}b \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{x}{b}_{x}+{a}_{y}{b}_{y}+{a}_{z}{b}_{z}}{{b}_{x}^{2}+{b}_{y}^{2}+{b}_{z}^{2}}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot 1+0\\cdot 5+1\\cdot (-1)}{{1}^{2}+{5}^{2}+(-1)^{2}}b \\\\  & =\\frac{0}{{1}^{2}+{5}^{2}+(-1)^{2}}b \\\\  & =⟨0,0,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186325812 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7c9317eb-d1ce-5f42-b69b-a37e643b865b" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Vector Projection Using Angle and Magnitude"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a40df457-c932-5555-aff1-534cb35483cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}b" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325814} {:answer/id #uuid "ff9db31d-0a43-57c5-8e40-0f5a4e8ca713" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}b" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325815} {:answer/id #uuid "3817e669-6cf2-5e7b-9eb0-b8235840dbc7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "b" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325816} {:answer/id #uuid "226553df-249e-5602-b374-cd5a145abff8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}b" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325817} {:answer/id #uuid "fd2b00b5-25d4-5da2-9b6d-d9841eb827d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}b" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325818}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a40df457-c932-5555-aff1-534cb35483cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}b" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325814} :answer-field/id #uuid "485c6674-fab3-5f38-a6f9-36bf4a4f7ad4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325813}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c0285a1e-a5cf-5cc8-a08b-5240464d9ec8" :question/math-academy-id "q-18375" :question/problem "Suppose that $|\\,a\\,|=6$, $|\\,b\\,|=2$ and that the angle between the vectors is $\\theta =\\frac{\\pi }{3}.$ Find the vector projection of $a$ onto $b$ in terms of the vector $b.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the scalar projection as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{b}\\,a & =|\\,a\\,|\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =6\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3}) \\\\  & =6\\cdot \\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the unit vector that is parallel to $b:$\n\n$$\nu=\\frac{b}{|\\,b\\,|}=\\frac{b}{2}=\\frac{1}{2}b\n$$\n\nFinally, we compute the vector projection as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{b}\\,a & ={\\text{comp}}_{b}\\,a\\cdot u \\\\  & =3\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}b \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}b\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278138 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c0670172-77cb-5e88-b78d-e5136c06095f" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Vector Projection Using Components"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bb5b189a-a239-5470-8788-4faacd32cb38" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨3\\sqrt{2},3,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278140} {:answer/id #uuid "1433dd63-e106-5e2a-a9b0-9d596b00d07f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,0,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278141} {:answer/id #uuid "b7c2e29b-7068-557b-8cc7-55acec4330b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-\\sqrt{2},-1,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278142} {:answer/id #uuid "a0b259a5-5948-5fc3-a399-efeadb1bb56f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,-\\frac{9}{4},-\\frac{3}{4}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278143} {:answer/id #uuid "bc3df04f-5c06-5456-a867-4e13c336b9aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-\\sqrt{2},1,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278144}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b7c2e29b-7068-557b-8cc7-55acec4330b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-\\sqrt{2},-1,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278142} :answer-field/id #uuid "3d280dbb-b209-5df3-8069-73c3ea8485e2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278139}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b8e013a5-b3de-5807-ade4-01f7026dfed4" :question/math-academy-id "q-18377" :question/problem "Let $a=⟨0,-3,1⟩$ and $b=⟨\\sqrt{2},1,0⟩.$ Find the vector projection of $a$ onto $b.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the formula for the vector projection, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{b}\\,a & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{b\\cdot b}b \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{x}{b}_{x}+{a}_{y}{b}_{y}+{a}_{z}{b}_{z}}{{b}_{x}^{2}+{b}_{y}^{2}+{b}_{z}^{2}}b \\\\  & =\\frac{0\\cdot \\sqrt{2}+(-3)\\cdot 1+1\\cdot 0}{(\\sqrt{2})^{2}+{1}^{2}+{0}^{2}}b \\\\  & =\\frac{-3}{3}⟨\\sqrt{2},1,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\sqrt{2},-1,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186285221 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c0670172-77cb-5e88-b78d-e5136c06095f" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Vector Projection Using Components"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2c11326f-5909-58ab-8ac9-a2e6eac5d144" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-\\frac{7}{9},\\frac{2}{9},-\\frac{1}{9}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285223} {:answer/id #uuid "012048d7-8f85-51ed-a130-8530ce2575cc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,0,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285224} {:answer/id #uuid "2183e8b9-c1ec-59aa-86ca-a75255ee33c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-\\frac{7}{54},\\frac{2}{54},-\\frac{1}{54}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285225} {:answer/id #uuid "e9782f45-163f-53f2-b62b-0bb67425f1b0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-\\frac{7}{54},\\frac{2}{9},-\\frac{1}{54}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285226} {:answer/id #uuid "7e664081-7f20-570b-8217-9fab34b88008" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{2}{9},-\\frac{7}{9},\\frac{1}{9}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285227}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2c11326f-5909-58ab-8ac9-a2e6eac5d144" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-\\frac{7}{9},\\frac{2}{9},-\\frac{1}{9}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285223} :answer-field/id #uuid "e63f8760-8604-5eea-a72f-ab9fa16b5226" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285222}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "06e573d1-988c-580b-8411-4633e9b41f74" :question/math-academy-id "q-19211" :question/problem "Let $a=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]$ and $b=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$ Find the vector projection of $a$ onto $b.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the formula for the vector projection, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{b}\\,a & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{b\\cdot b}b \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{x}{b}_{x}+{a}_{y}{b}_{y}+{a}_{z}{b}_{z}}{{b}_{x}^{2}+{b}_{y}^{2}+{b}_{z}^{2}}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot 7+8\\cdot (-2)+3\\cdot 1}{{7}^{2}+(-2)^{2}+{1}^{2}}b \\\\  & =-\\frac{6}{54}⟨7,-2,1⟩ \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{9}⟨7,-2,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{7}{9},\\frac{2}{9},-\\frac{1}{9}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186325819 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "84c96375-27d5-5ada-a952-34e09b3e92bf" :knowledge-point/title "Perpendicular Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b4403445-67b9-5876-9621-ce0068b1361b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325821} {:answer/id #uuid "0d164dc5-be40-53e4-a218-e773477db450" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325822} {:answer/id #uuid "1f724f5d-1017-5aef-a991-2e192949147c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325823} {:answer/id #uuid "ed41853b-dbb8-5c31-a285-e39712881dca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325824} {:answer/id #uuid "5f08c71b-e3ae-5e32-9780-1d0a1289f475" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325825}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1f724f5d-1017-5aef-a991-2e192949147c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325823} :answer-field/id #uuid "9b194a7c-3083-53f0-aefe-7c4fa914ccff" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325820}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6c4a1fe8-f923-59d1-9b70-b2a00cdbb8f6" :question/math-academy-id "q-212206" :question/problem "Let $a=⟨1,2,3⟩$ and $b=⟨2,-3,x⟩.$ Given that the projection of $a$ onto $b$ is the zero vector, find the value of $x.$" :question/worked-solution "Since $a$ is a nonzero vector, its projection onto another nonzero vector $b$ equals the zero vector only when the vectors are perpendicular. \n\nSo, we must have\n\n$$\na⊥b\\,⟹\\,a\\cdot b=0.\n$$\n\nComputing the dot product, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b & ={a}_{x}\\cdot {b}_{x}+{a}_{y}\\cdot {b}_{y}+{a}_{z}\\cdot {b}_{z} \\\\  & =1\\cdot 2+2\\cdot (-3)+3\\cdot x \\\\  & =3x-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting the dot product equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b & =0 \\\\ 3x-4 & =0 \\\\ 3x & =4 \\\\ x & =\\frac{4}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186325826 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "84c96375-27d5-5ada-a952-34e09b3e92bf" :knowledge-point/title "Perpendicular Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "43fcfd16-71ee-58fc-b316-7659097da4b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325828} {:answer/id #uuid "81cfbe15-9ef7-5c75-b32f-308be5763311" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325829} {:answer/id #uuid "d1859c9b-d292-5956-94ba-f9dda7386eab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325830} {:answer/id #uuid "29b28e6d-d280-5ea3-90b5-387423d3de2a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325831} {:answer/id #uuid "6baa0b47-46fe-5dfa-b7bf-c59e3a2817fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325832}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d1859c9b-d292-5956-94ba-f9dda7386eab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325830} :answer-field/id #uuid "68a3c741-9a0b-5a47-9302-8c9bdf985cc2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325827}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9f6200bc-fe43-56c7-ac3d-8a648cdf9316" :question/math-academy-id "q-212456" :question/problem "Let $a=⟨-2,3,1⟩$ and $b=⟨-1,-2,x⟩.$ Given that the projection of $a$ onto $b$ is the zero vector, find the value of $x.$" :question/worked-solution "Since $a$ is a nonzero vector, its projection onto another nonzero vector $b$ equals the zero vector only when the vectors are perpendicular. \n\nSo, we must have\n\n$$\na⊥b\\,⟹\\,a\\cdot b=0.\n$$\n\nComputing the dot product, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b & ={a}_{x}\\cdot {b}_{x}+{a}_{y}\\cdot {b}_{y}+{a}_{z}\\cdot {b}_{z} \\\\  & =-2\\cdot (-1)+3\\cdot (-2)+1\\cdot x \\\\  & =x-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting the dot product equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b & =0 \\\\ x-4 & =0 \\\\ x & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186325833 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "84c96375-27d5-5ada-a952-34e09b3e92bf" :knowledge-point/title "Perpendicular Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c5e703e0-9ecb-5690-943b-c7c510abf491" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325835} {:answer/id #uuid "0b205f21-bc89-5ac8-ab11-acc61b483f46" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325836} {:answer/id #uuid "eee9127f-b4c5-5605-8394-d8aee8ba5a13" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325837} {:answer/id #uuid "8520b09f-4c02-5433-84c4-2067d3793c08" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325838} {:answer/id #uuid "df58f5f2-0605-56c6-a541-4df174d012cf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325839}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c5e703e0-9ecb-5690-943b-c7c510abf491" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325835} :answer-field/id #uuid "dd34f353-c15f-53df-b1eb-1e4a2cbbfee9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325834}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "28160526-4d46-5bbc-86fb-79ce8277111a" :question/math-academy-id "q-212462" :question/problem "Let $a=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]$ and $b=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ x\\end{aligned}].$ Given that the projection of $a$ onto $b$ is the zero vector, find the value of $x.$" :question/worked-solution "Since $a$ is a nonzero vector, its projection onto another nonzero vector $b$ equals the zero vector only when the vectors are perpendicular. \n\nSo, we must have\n\n$$\na⊥b\\,⟹\\,a\\cdot b=0.\n$$\n\nComputing the dot product, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b & ={a}_{x}\\cdot {b}_{x}+{a}_{y}\\cdot {b}_{y}+{a}_{z}\\cdot {b}_{z} \\\\  & =1\\cdot 1+3\\cdot (-2)+2\\cdot x \\\\  & =2x-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting the dot product equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b & =0 \\\\ 2x-5 & =0 \\\\ 2x & =5 \\\\ x & =\\frac{5}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186325840 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7c9317eb-d1ce-5f42-b69b-a37e643b865b" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Vector Projection Using Angle and Magnitude"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "862e3e33-0879-58d4-9652-f7d80110716e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4\\sqrt{2}}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325842}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "862e3e33-0879-58d4-9652-f7d80110716e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4\\sqrt{2}}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325842} :answer-field/id #uuid "13e10029-59bf-5a97-b9e9-494663c4d23e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325841}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "daea58c3-d874-52b1-9fd3-270fce74234d" :question/math-academy-id "q-275226" :question/problem "Suppose that $|\\,c\\,|=8$, $|\\,d\\,|=5$ and that the angle between the vectors is $\\theta ={45}^{∘}.$ Find the vector projection of $c$ onto $d$ in terms of the vector $d.$\n\n${\\text{proj}}_{d}\\,c=$\n{{field-1}}\n$d$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the scalar projection as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{d}\\,c & =|\\,c\\,|\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =8\\operatorname{cos}⁡({45}^{∘}) \\\\  & =8\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\  & =4\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the unit vector that is parallel to $d:$\n\n$$\nu=\\frac{d}{|\\,d\\,|}=\\frac{d}{5}=\\frac{1}{5}d\n$$\n\nFinally, we compute the vector projection as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{d}\\,c & ={\\text{comp}}_{d}\\,c\\cdot u \\\\  & =4\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{5}d \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\sqrt{2}}{5}\\,d\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278170 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c0670172-77cb-5e88-b78d-e5136c06095f" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Vector Projection Using Components"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e15fe54c-65a3-5c95-bde0-75492747c438" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278172} {:answer/id #uuid "7541c8ad-38ab-5c2f-ac90-24aa4e64367b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278173}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7541c8ad-38ab-5c2f-ac90-24aa4e64367b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278173} :answer-field/id #uuid "12f32dd3-ed56-5374-8c14-6d495b8663ea" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278171} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "619599e1-e9bd-5cbd-bc65-bf0146fc09c0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278175}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "619599e1-e9bd-5cbd-bc65-bf0146fc09c0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278175} :answer-field/id #uuid "1b650bda-a627-56ef-bab2-a99e8db80137" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278174} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4fd3150e-167c-53cf-939d-b549cc2303e2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{35}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278177}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4fd3150e-167c-53cf-939d-b549cc2303e2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{35}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278177} :answer-field/id #uuid "b9892346-cf69-5ae3-b300-41cbbc14982e" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278176}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "af7b2065-ddd7-541d-b600-09c9bbc528d5" :question/math-academy-id "q-275230" :question/problem "Let $c=⟨2,-1,6⟩$ and $d=⟨4,-2,10⟩.$ Find the vector projection of $c$ onto $d.$\n\n${\\text{proj}}_{d}\\,c=⟨$\n{{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}$,$\n{{field-3}}\n$⟩$" :question/worked-solution "Using the formula for the vector projection, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{d}\\,c & =\\frac{c\\cdot d}{d\\cdot d}d \\\\  & =\\frac{{c}_{x}{d}_{x}+{c}_{y}{d}_{y}+{c}_{z}{d}_{z}}{{d}_{x}^{2}+{d}_{y}^{2}+{d}_{z}^{2}}d \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\cdot 4+(-1)\\cdot (-2)+6\\cdot 10}{{4}^{2}+(-2)^{2}+{10}^{2}}d \\\\  & =\\frac{70}{120}⟨4,-2,10⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{12}⟨4,-2,10⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\,\\frac{7}{3},-\\frac{7}{6},\\frac{35}{6}\\,⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278192 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "84c96375-27d5-5ada-a952-34e09b3e92bf" :knowledge-point/title "Perpendicular Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3d6cefe9-ad1a-5c96-89ee-13765cab6bdc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278194} {:answer/id #uuid "b2f9ca16-7042-569a-baeb-d1ce8d29aa01" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278195}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3d6cefe9-ad1a-5c96-89ee-13765cab6bdc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278194} :answer-field/id #uuid "8e7fdc11-8a2f-532b-9337-bd8dcc7ccf8f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278193}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ba2dc2b6-282e-5a04-8a40-e8efff6fe0f3" :question/math-academy-id "q-275237" :question/problem "Let $a=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]$ and $b=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$ Given that the projection of $a$ onto $b$ is the zero vector, find the value of $x.$\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Since $a$ is a nonzero vector, its projection onto another nonzero vector $b$ equals the zero vector only when the vectors are perpendicular. \n\nSo, we must have\n\n$$\na⊥b\\,⟹\\,a\\cdot b=0.\n$$\n\nComputing the dot product, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b & ={a}_{x}\\cdot {b}_{x}+{a}_{y}\\cdot {b}_{y}+{a}_{z}\\cdot {b}_{z} \\\\  & =-2\\cdot x+1\\cdot 3+2\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-2x+5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting the dot product equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b & =0 \\\\ -2x+5 & =0 \\\\ 2x & =5 \\\\ x & =\\frac{5}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186325843 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7c9317eb-d1ce-5f42-b69b-a37e643b865b" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Vector Projection Using Angle and Magnitude"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1dcc6997-18c5-522e-881b-7cd4e1484779" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325845}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1dcc6997-18c5-522e-881b-7cd4e1484779" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325845} :answer-field/id #uuid "8a4e0f91-106a-569f-8ca1-3f154f056429" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325844}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a092a38f-400b-570a-acab-c1982ddee78b" :question/math-academy-id "q-316436" :question/problem "Suppose that $|\\,m\\,|=12$, $|\\,n\\,|=9$ and that the angle between the vectors is $\\theta ={30}^{∘}.$ Find the vector projection of $m$ onto $n$ in terms of the vector $n.$\n\n${\\text{proj}}_{n}\\,m=$\n{{field-1}}\n$n$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the scalar projection as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,m & =|\\,m\\,|\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =12\\operatorname{cos}⁡({30}^{∘}) \\\\  & =12\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\\\  & =6\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the unit vector that is parallel to $n:$\n\n$$\nu=\\frac{n}{|\\,n\\,|}=\\frac{n}{9}=\\frac{1}{9}n\n$$\n\nFinally, we compute the vector projection as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{n}\\,m & ={\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,m\\cdot u \\\\  & =6\\sqrt{3}\\cdot \\frac{1}{9}n \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{3}n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186325846 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c0670172-77cb-5e88-b78d-e5136c06095f" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Vector Projection Using Components"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9608e208-cc08-5c25-8d14-7d6e9268f051" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{33}{14}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325848}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9608e208-cc08-5c25-8d14-7d6e9268f051" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{33}{14}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325848} :answer-field/id #uuid "dd2dbf9c-17c0-5475-a059-4faac3b1d390" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325847} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0011cd6d-710f-52fe-9d83-21d7865fb4a9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325850}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0011cd6d-710f-52fe-9d83-21d7865fb4a9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325850} :answer-field/id #uuid "a5f16061-71ff-5c16-a2dd-21a4d12382f5" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325849} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9829534a-4f1d-5319-abba-0c9b1c096a26" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{11}{14}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325852}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9829534a-4f1d-5319-abba-0c9b1c096a26" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{11}{14}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325852} :answer-field/id #uuid "2f2f934a-0c8d-52b8-976e-e453560dfaeb" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325851}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "cd0cbfc6-b126-54ce-bf9b-c834946584f4" :question/math-academy-id "q-316469" :question/problem "Let $c=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ and $d=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].$ Find the vector projection of $d$ onto $c.$\n\n${\\text{proj}}_{c}\\,d=⟨$  \n\n{{field-1}},\n\n{{field-2}},\n\n{{field-3}}\n\n$⟩$" :question/worked-solution "Using the formula for the vector projection, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{c}\\,d & =\\frac{c\\cdot d}{c\\cdot c}c \\\\  & =\\frac{{c}_{x}{d}_{x}+{c}_{y}{d}_{y}+{c}_{z}{d}_{z}}{{c}_{x}^{2}+{c}_{y}^{2}+{c}_{z}^{2}}c \\\\  & =\\frac{(3)(0)+(-2)(5)+(1)(-1)}{{3}^{2}+(-2)^{2}+{1}^{2}}c \\\\  & =\\frac{0-10-1}{9+4+1}\\,⟨3,-2,1⟩ \\\\  & =-\\frac{11}{14}\\,⟨3,-2,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{33}{14},\\frac{11}{7},-\\frac{11}{14}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n`"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106408 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "84c96375-27d5-5ada-a952-34e09b3e92bf" :knowledge-point/title "Perpendicular Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f0b5d2f2-111b-5f36-9574-2bddbaa91b43" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{30}},-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{30}},-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{30}}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186104958} {:answer/id #uuid "f4f58996-7c81-5e9f-ba8e-db6242aefc7d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}},-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}, \\sqrt{5}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186104959} {:answer/id #uuid "35a3fa91-2877-5f05-a29d-c67415825e7c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0, 0, 0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186104960} {:answer/id #uuid "46105738-53e5-5544-b410-1c5c6a0dca2a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186104961} {:answer/id #uuid "4e7f5cbb-14b3-506f-adb0-22b07a0eede9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{5}},-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}},-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186104962}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "35a3fa91-2877-5f05-a29d-c67415825e7c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0, 0, 0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186104960} :answer-field/id #uuid "c2b6ad5b-aaf4-500d-b96a-7b1a0906a3f4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186104957}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ab29d467-5294-537a-b48f-a1d1aefe0cab" :question/math-academy-id "q-71668" :question/problem "Let $a=⟨1,-2,5⟩$ and $b=⟨3,-1,-1⟩.$ Find the vector projection of $a$ onto $b.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the formula for the vector projection, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{b}\\,a & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{b\\cdot b}b \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{x}{b}_{x}+{a}_{y}{b}_{y}+{a}_{z}{b}_{z}}{{b}_{x}^{2}+{b}_{y}^{2}+{b}_{z}^{2}}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot 3+(-2)\\cdot (-1)+5\\cdot (-1)}{{3}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+(-1)^{2}}b \\\\  & =\\frac{0}{{3}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+(-1)^{2}}b \\\\  & =⟨0,0,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186325853 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c0670172-77cb-5e88-b78d-e5136c06095f" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Vector Projection Using Components"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7bac7e28-9988-5e7f-b9d7-ed23463d9212" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-1,-2,3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325855} {:answer/id #uuid "dcf18d83-3a17-55ba-b80d-3b6fc9123d1c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-3,-1,2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325856} {:answer/id #uuid "9bf49c87-908c-5b8e-ba91-3f7e507ae54d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-4,-2,6⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325857} {:answer/id #uuid "a3a24283-48ef-5cb5-933a-bd38287e7999" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-2,-1,3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325858} {:answer/id #uuid "97458e17-fc00-5e60-9314-1d629e85b448" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-6,-2,4⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325859}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a3a24283-48ef-5cb5-933a-bd38287e7999" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-2,-1,3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325858} :answer-field/id #uuid "3d9c70cb-2a4e-5dbb-a309-4c6cf958beea" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325854}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "06286d73-225f-5331-8e6a-d04051a18b14" :question/math-academy-id "q-71834" :question/problem "Let $c=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]$ and $d=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}].$ Find the vector projection of $d$ onto $c.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the formula for the vector projection, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{c}\\,d & =\\frac{c\\cdot d}{c\\cdot c}c \\\\  & =\\frac{{c}_{x}{d}_{x}+{c}_{y}{d}_{y}+{c}_{z}{d}_{z}}{{c}_{x}^{2}+{c}_{y}^{2}+{c}_{z}^{2}}c \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\cdot 2+1\\cdot (-3)+(-3)\\cdot 5}{{2}^{2}+{1}^{2}+(-3)^{2}}c \\\\  & =-\\frac{14}{14}⟨2,1,-3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2,-1,3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278217 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7c9317eb-d1ce-5f42-b69b-a37e643b865b" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Vector Projection Using Angle and Magnitude"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ece23503-bd50-5b21-94c0-5a21dd3f5a7e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}d" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278219} {:answer/id #uuid "b2f3bbbd-559f-5e27-9190-64dc733578f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5d" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278220} {:answer/id #uuid "01bacc67-0858-554d-a2ad-adfed5f8dc32" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}d" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278221} {:answer/id #uuid "f6da54aa-6722-520c-8d57-601765094e27" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{5}d" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278222} {:answer/id #uuid "1d7ffe4d-4b39-59ef-b4ff-61a6dce957f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5\\sqrt{3}}{3}d" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278223}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "01bacc67-0858-554d-a2ad-adfed5f8dc32" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}d" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278221} :answer-field/id #uuid "5c9ee979-e0da-5150-9eaf-e21e2bc6decb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278218}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7ba84402-0df7-51f8-9c09-70d13a0fe926" :question/math-academy-id "q-71838" :question/problem "Suppose that $|\\,c\\,|=10$, $|\\,d\\,|=2\\sqrt{3}$ and that the angle between the vectors is $\\theta ={30}^{∘}.$ Find the vector projection of $c$ onto $d$ in terms of the vector $d.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the scalar projection as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{d}\\,c & =|\\,c\\,|\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =10\\operatorname{cos}⁡({30}^{∘}) \\\\  & =10\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\\\  & =5\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the unit vector that is parallel to $d:$\n\n$$\nu=\\frac{d}{|\\,d\\,|}=\\frac{d}{2\\sqrt{3}}=\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{3}}d\n$$\n\nFinally, we compute the vector projection as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{d}\\,c & ={\\text{comp}}_{d}\\,c\\cdot u \\\\  & =5\\sqrt{3}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{3}}d \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}d\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186325860 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7c9317eb-d1ce-5f42-b69b-a37e643b865b" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Vector Projection Using Angle and Magnitude"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1eaf1eed-0496-58dc-9c75-cff822674ba5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4p" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325862} {:answer/id #uuid "e890ca52-bb85-57e8-aeae-c7df14541488" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2p" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325863} {:answer/id #uuid "004b0b9a-dde8-55c8-bca0-cc1dfaf19285" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}p" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325864} {:answer/id #uuid "5157be96-2b36-5c33-9ffa-ac7acc3a23fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{2}p" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325865} {:answer/id #uuid "0e8958b9-bf07-53aa-a467-fe7365b3ceeb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}p" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325866}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e890ca52-bb85-57e8-aeae-c7df14541488" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2p" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325863} :answer-field/id #uuid "e8d5b1a1-10b3-507b-a78b-6c3a79b92eb9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325861}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3a30c492-7d0c-5812-875a-26f65ee34ae6" :question/math-academy-id "q-71839" :question/problem "Suppose that $|\\,p\\,|=4\\sqrt{2}$, $|\\,q\\,|=16$ and that the angle between the vectors is $\\theta ={45}^{∘}.$ Find the vector projection of $q$ onto $p$ in terms of the vector $p.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the scalar projection as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{p}\\,q & =|\\,q\\,|\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =16\\operatorname{cos}⁡({45}^{∘}) \\\\  & =16\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\  & =8\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the unit vector that is parallel to $p:$\n\n$$\nu=\\frac{p}{|\\,p\\,|}=\\frac{p}{4\\sqrt{2}}=\\frac{1}{4\\sqrt{2}}p\n$$\n\nFinally, we compute the vector projection as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{p}\\,q & ={\\text{comp}}_{p}\\,q\\cdot u \\\\  & =8\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{4\\sqrt{2}}p \\\\  & =2p\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
